From: Wazo Support <support@wazo.io>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audiohook: rebuild read translation path on slin rate change

audiohook_read_frame_helper() caches the translation path used to
convert the hook's slin frames to the requested format, and only
rebuilds it when the requested format changes. The path is built from
the hook's slin format at that moment, but the hook's internal rate can
change afterwards (e.g. a call transferred to a channel using a codec
with a higher sample rate). The stale path then converts the new frames
as if they were at the old rate, so MixMonitor recordings are
frequency-shifted after the change.

Also rebuild the path when its source sample rate differs from the
hook's current slin rate.

Not reproduced on a live call yet.
---
 main/audiohook.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

Index: asterisk-22.11.0/main/audiohook.c
===================================================================
--- asterisk-22.11.0.orig/main/audiohook.c
+++ asterisk-22.11.0/main/audiohook.c
@@ -681,8 +681,10 @@
 
 	/* If they don't want signed linear back out, we'll have to send it through the translation path */
 	if (ast_format_cmp(format, slin) != AST_FORMAT_CMP_EQUAL) {
-		/* Rebuild translation path if different format then previously */
-		if (ast_format_cmp(format, audiohook->format) == AST_FORMAT_CMP_NOT_EQUAL) {
+		/* Rebuild translation path if different format or slin rate then previously */
+		if (ast_format_cmp(format, audiohook->format) == AST_FORMAT_CMP_NOT_EQUAL
+			|| !audiohook->trans_pvt
+			|| audiohook->trans_pvt->t->src_codec.sample_rate != ast_format_get_sample_rate(slin)) {
 			if (audiohook->trans_pvt) {
 				ast_translator_free_path(audiohook->trans_pvt);
 				audiohook->trans_pvt = NULL;
